Practice Data Analysis in Microsoft Excel

This repository contains a collection of Excel exercises focused on learning and practicing essential data analysis techniques using Microsoft Excel. The workbook demonstrates real-world data preparation, text manipulation, statistical analysis, lookup functions, conditional formulas, and reporting through Pivot Tables and charts.

### Topics Covered:

- Data Cleaning and Formatting
- Text Functions (CONCAT, PROPER, UPPER, LOWER)
- Date Extraction Functions
- IF Statements and Logical Functions
- Statistical Functions (SUM, AVERAGE, MEDIAN, MODE)
- Conditional Functions (SUMIF, COUNTIF, AVERAGEIF, SUMIFS, COUNTIFS)
- Text to Columns (Data Splitting)
- VLOOKUP and MATCH Functions
- Pivot Tables
- Basic Data Visualization

### Learning Objectives:

- Prepare and clean structured datasets
- Perform statistical and conditional analysis
- Retrieve data efficiently using lookup functions
- Summarize large datasets with Pivot Tables
- Build a strong foundation for Excel-based data analysis

This workbook serves as a hands-on practice project for beginners and aspiring data analysts who want to strengthen their Microsoft Excel skills before moving to advanced tools such as Power BI, SQL, Python, and Tableau.
